### 8. They compute inside one specialty and never ask for closure

For this repository the relevant specialty is computational chemistry.

**Why it is stupid.** The equations for an atom or a molecule have been known since the 1920s. The field
answered by fitting: parameters adjusted until outputs match measured or previously computed numbers, with no
proof of error on any result. Each number is a guess of unknown quality, nothing composes into a guaranteed
